Column name: msa_geom Type: BINARY Description: Points of a polygon that encompass the state. Should be used for geographic visualization
Column name: csa_code Type: TEXT Description: Current Combined Statistical Area (CSA) code of the CSA that contains the metropolitan statistical area/micropolitan statistical area (MSA)
Column name: int_point_lat Type: TEXT Description: Current latitude of the internal point, which is the point at or closest to the MSA's geographic center
Column name: name Type: TEXT Description: Full text name of the metropolitan statistical area/micropolitan statistical area
Column name: msa_code Type: TEXT Description: Current metropolitan statistical area/micropolitan
statistical area (MSA) code
Column name: int_point_lon Type: TEXT Description: Current longitude of the internal point, which is the point at or closest to the MSA's geographic center
Column name: area_water_meters Type: NUMBER Description: Current water area, in square meters
Column name: status_indicator Type: TEXT Description: Current metropolitan/micropolitan status indicator. 

1 indicates a metropolitan statistical area. Each metropolitan statistical area must have at least one urbanized area of 50,000 or more inhabitants.
2 indicates a micropolitan statistical area. Each micropolitan statistical area must have at least one urban cluster of at least 10,000 inhabitants, with no more than 49,999
Column name: area_land_meters Type: NUMBER Description: Current land area, in square meters
Column name: lsad_code Type: TEXT Description: Legal/Statistical area description (LSAD) code for a given MSA.

M1 indicates a "metro area (suffix)"
M2 indicates a "micro area (suffix)"
Column name: lsad_name Type: TEXT Description: Current name and the translated legal/statistical area description for metropolitan statistical area/micropolitan statistical area
Column name: feature_class_code Type: TEXT Description: MAF/TIGER feature class code 

G3110 indicates either a metropolitan or micropolitan statistical area
Column name: geo_code Type: TEXT Description: Unique identifier for each MSA. Matches msa_code
